task: fs2-chunked-merge-lanes
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/fs2-chunked-merge-lanes
worktree: ../okay-wt-fs2

why: every fs2 row in §6 and §6b is fed from `fs2.Stream.range`, which
  in 3.10.2 is `emit(o) ++ go(o + step)` -- a singleton chunk per
  element (Stream.scala:3981). So the "chunk-native fs2" row (44 443)
  is not chunk-native, the "matched 16" row chunks AFTER the merge,
  and the singleton row is the only honest one. benchmark-fairness-
  audit measured chunking BEFORE the merge at N=2000: 281 vs 35 700.

what: feed the fs2 lanes from `Stream.emits` (fs2's own one-chunk
  source, per its scaladoc), chunk BEFORE the merge for the matched-k
  row, keep the old lanes renamed as the diagnostics they are, and
  re-pair §6 (N=500) and §6b (N=2000) at their own N. Not scaled.
